cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ShopSphere: Cloud-Based E-Commerce Platform Using AWS Cloud Architecture"
message: >-
  If you reference this project in academic work or course evaluations, please cite it using the metadata below.
  Supervised by Dr. S Vigneshwari (Faculty Supervisor, School of Computer Science and Engineering,
  Vellore Institute of Technology, Chennai) for BCSE355L Cloud Architecture Design (Direct Assessment III).
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-25"
url: "https://d2yj8h74tzry42.cloudfront.net/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/AdityaNarayan1212/ShopSphere"
abstract: >-
  ShopSphere is a full-stack cloud-based e-commerce web application developed for BCSE355L Cloud Architecture Design
  (Direct Assessment III) at Vellore Institute of Technology, Chennai. The platform is deployed on Amazon Web Services
  (ap-south-1) using Amazon CloudFront for HTTPS delivery and path-based routing, a single Ubuntu 24.04 EC2 instance
  running Nginx and PM2-managed Express.js, a private Single-AZ Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL instance, an IAM instance
  profile for credential-free AWS SDK access, a private Amazon S3 bucket (shopsphere-products-2026) for presigned
  product image uploads, and Amazon SNS for order notifications.
